------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(2) THE MASS-INDEPENDENCE TEST  (convention-invariant)
    n = 11 clusters with sigma_gal (A644 excluded, no published value located)
    log10(sigma_gal/sigma_gas,1d): mean -0.008  median -0.001  rms 0.0621 dex  MAD 0.0368 dex  range [-0.134, +0.117]
    (task formula: identical numbers, values shifted by -log10(sqrt3) = -0.239)
    Spearman rho(log10 R vs log10 M500) = -0.518 (p = 0.069, two-sided, t-approx)
    OLS slope d log10R / d log10 M500 = -0.118 +- 0.139 (consistent with 0 at 0.8 sigma)
    A1d[A85] = 0.954  -> beta = -0.37
    A1d[A1644] = 1.000  -> beta = -0.00
    A1d[A1795] = 0.844  -> beta = -6.45
    A1d[A2029] = 0.735  (no physical constant-beta SIS value: A^2 < 2/3)
    A1d[A2142] = 0.917  -> beta = -0.91
    A1d[A2255] = 1.000  -> beta = -0.00
    A1d[A2319] = 1.310  -> beta = +0.68
    A1d[A3158] = 1.104  -> beta = +0.40
    A1d[A3266] = 0.998  -> beta = -0.01
    A1d[RXC1825] = 1.099  -> beta = +0.39
    A1d[ZW1215] = 0.938  -> beta = -0.57

    cluster ratios in the P6 band (1.0, 1.6): 3/11 (R3d footing: 0/11 -- the sqrt(3) is the 1D->3D gas conversion, not anisotropy)
    cluster ratios in the V2 band (0.9, 1.7): 9/11
    median A (1d footing) = 0.998;  SIS-inverted median beta = -0.00 (n phys = 10);  A<1 <-> tangential, A>1 <-> radial
    plausibility: beta ~ 0 - 0.5 typical for cluster galaxies (e.g.
    Lokas+06 fitted beta ~ 0.00 for A3158; Munari+13/Biviano+13: mild radial in outskirts); the A-star outliers are the flagged out-of-equilibrium systems (A2319, A3266, RXC1825) and A2029/A1795 (A ~ 0.73-0.84).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(4) THE VERDICTS
  V1 [spread < 0.2 dex]: rms = 0.0621 dex -> PASS  (|spearman rho| = 0.518 (trend flag))
      both footings identical; robustness vs the sigma_gal source choice is +-0.05-0.10 dex (see cross-checks below)
  V2 [implied anisotropy factor in (0.9, 1.7)]: median A1d = 0.998, 9/11 clusters in band -> PASS  (band-footing 1D-vs-1D; task-formula footing: A/sqrt3 ~ 0.576 -- outside (0.9,1.7) by construction)
  V3 [the honest statement]: the cross-instrument equipartition sigma_gal,los ~ sigma_gas,1d = sqrt(kT/mu m_p) HOLDS (median A = 0.998, i.e. deviation from isotropic equipartition -0.002, SIS-inverted beta ~ -0.00 -- mildly aniso, consistent with measured cluster beta)
  V3-context: under the task's literal sigma_gas = sqrt(3kT/mu m_p) the ratios sit at 0.576 ~ 0.6-0.9 -- the equipartition, read as sigma_gal,los vs the gas 3D rms, fails the 'ratio ~ 1' form by the Maxwellian sqrt(3), which is a convention, not physics.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
